# The change list remembers where the last change happened; for an
# append that is the last inserted char. Neovim 0.12.5 (keys typed):
# `2GAX<Esc>5GAY<Esc>gg g; g; iZ<Esc>` -> line 2 = "l2ZX" (g; lands ON
# the X).
write f.txt "l1\nl2\nl3\nl4\nl5\nl6\n"
open f.txt
command editor.use_vim
type "2GAX"
key escape
type "5GAY"
key escape
type "ggg;g;iZ"
key escape
ex w
expect file f.txt contains "l2ZX\n"
